{
  "rationale": "This is iteration 0, so there is no race telemetry or integration feedback yet. The design therefore rests on the contract's physics. To finish in under 3 s the robot needs an average of about 1.5 m/s, so I want full drive authority and low inertia. Lower mass (0.6 kg) helps acceleration and braking through bends. A 0.03 m wheel radius gives reasonable top speed at full PWM. A 0.12 m wheel track keeps turn authority reasonable without making the yaw response sluggish. Five sensors spread across +/-0.03 m with 12 mm footprints overlap the 25 mm tape at all times, so the line is never lost while the robot is centred and the signal stays smooth. The sensors sit 0.07 m ahead of the axle so the robot reacts to the line before the wheels reach a bend. The body is 0.12 m wide, which keeps the off-track limit at its 0.06 m minimum. I'm deliberately leaving the body envelope at a middle value, since it has no dynamic effect. Expected result: a first completion on the oval with low rms error. The main risks are oscillation on the slalom and speed-limited bends, which the Integrator's feedback should expose.",
  "geometry": {
    "sensor_positions": [
      {"x": 0.03, "y": 0.07},
      {"x": 0.015, "y": 0.07},
      {"x": 0.0, "y": 0.07},
      {"x": -0.015, "y": 0.07},
      {"x": -0.03, "y": 0.07}
    ],
    "sensor_size": 0.012,
    "wheel_track": 0.12,
    "wheel_radius": 0.03,
    "body_width": 0.12,
    "body_length": 0.16,
    "mass": 0.6
  },
  "intent": "Establish a symmetric, forward-mounted five-sensor array with a 12 mm footprint that always covers the 25 mm tape, a light chassis for acceleration, and a 0.03 m wheel radius for speed. Expect a first completed run with moderate rms error. Use the next race to see whether the geometry limits speed on bends or causes oscillation, and adjust sensor spacing or mass accordingly.",
  "feedback_request": {
    "questions": [
      "Does the five-sensor spread at +/-0.03 m with 12 mm footprints give a usable, non-saturated signal through the sharpest bend, or do sensors lose the line at the edges?",
      "Is the 0.07 m forward offset too far ahead for stable tracking, or does it help anticipate bends?",
      "Does the 0.6 kg mass and 0.03 m wheel radius reach the speed needed to finish in under 3 s?",
      "Is the 0.12 m wheel track a limiting factor for turn rate on the slalom?"
    ],
    "measure_next": ["completion", "progress", "completion_time", "rms_error", "max_error", "line_loss_events", "steering_oscillation"]
  },
  "learning": "No prior evidence exists. Starting baseline. Next iteration should use the Integrator's controller-fit feedback and race telemetry to decide whether sensor spread, forward offset, mass, or wheel size is the limiting factor."
}
